gml_changes.why:
Keeping the remote body out of the objPlayer tree avoids:
- first-instance ambiguity in 3427 objPlayer.<var> references;
- with(objPlayer) kills of everyone;
- the code5320 duplicate check;
- restart gating on instance_exists(objPlayer);
- objPlayer Create/Step/Draw side effects;
- transitions (objTransitioner_Collision_98 only accepts the concrete player objects anyway);
- camera writes.
Door pushing is the one objPlayer behaviour wanted, so it is forwarded explicitly.

gml_changes.change:
Mechanical UTMT transform:
- prepend: var coop_t; coop_t = scrCoopTarget();
- replace READS of objPlayer.x and objPlayer.y (regex excluding assignment) with coop_t.x and coop_t.y;
- replace instance_exists(objPlayer) with instance_exists(coop_t).
Re-decompile and diff to verify.

